Return a narrow splitter width for the Dolphin status bar

Dolphin 26.08 takes the geometry of its small status bar from the style
in src/statusbar/dolphinstatusbar.cpp. The clippingAmount() function at
line 308 returns 2 pixels plus twice PM_SplitterWidth. Line 437 takes
two clipping amounts for the left margin of the layout, and one for the
right margin. Line 292 asks for the text width, plus one average
character width, plus two clipping amounts. Line 282 adds one clipping
amount to the minimum height of the bar. The full width status bar keeps
the fixed margins at line 434, and takes no clipping amount.

The label therefore keeps the text width, plus one average character
width, minus one clipping amount. Each pixel of the metric costs the
label 2 pixels of width. Each pixel also adds 2 pixels to the height of
the bar.

Breeze returns 1 pixel, so the clipping amount is 4 pixels. QtCurve
returns 7 pixels for the default line style of splitters, or 6 pixels
for the other styles. The clipping amount is then 16 or 14 pixels.

The Plasma default font is Noto Sans at 10 points. At 96 dots per inch
that font has an average character width of 8 pixels. It draws
"1 folder, 5 files (1.1 MiB)" in 144 pixels.

Breeze therefore gives the label 148 pixels, 4 more than the text needs.
QtCurve gives the label 136 pixels with the default line style, 8 less
than the text needs. The label then elides the text to
"1 folder, 5…s (1.1 MiB)". The bar is also 12 pixels taller.

Return the Breeze value of 1 pixel for the status bar widget. The small
bar then gets the Breeze geometry. The case for PM_SplitterWidth moves
above the case for PM_DockWidgetSeparatorExtent, so the test covers one
metric. Both metrics keep the shared return. Every other widget keeps
the QtCurve width, and a call with no widget keeps it too. Dolphin 26.08
uses Qt 6, so the identical block at qt5/style/qtcurve_api.cpp:1690
needs no change.

Drop this patch when Dolphin no longer takes its status bar geometry
from PM_SplitterWidth.

diff --git a/qt6/style/qtcurve_api.cpp b/qt6/style/qtcurve_api.cpp
index faf4880f..36b69e42 100644
--- a/qt6/style/qtcurve_api.cpp
+++ b/qt6/style/qtcurve_api.cpp
@@ -1685,8 +1685,15 @@ Style::pixelMetric(PixelMetric metric, const QStyleOption *option,
         return 4;
     // case PM_DockWindowHandleExtent:
     //     return 10;
-    case PM_DockWidgetSeparatorExtent:
     case PM_SplitterWidth:
+        // Dolphin takes the width, the margins and the minimum height
+        // of its small status bar from this metric. Each pixel of the
+        // metric costs the status label 2 pixels. The label then elides
+        // the text. Return 1 pixel, the Breeze value.
+        if (qtcCheckType(widget, "DolphinStatusBar"))
+            return 1;
+        QTC_FALLTHROUGH();
+    case PM_DockWidgetSeparatorExtent:
         return LINE_1DOT==opts.splitters ? 7 : 6;
     case PM_ToolBarHandleExtent:
         return LINE_1DOT==opts.handles ? 7 : 8;
